# 6. PRODUCT GALLERY — COMPLETE RECONSTRUCTION

Create:

`src/components/commerce/ProductGallery.astro`

This component is one of the primary visual elements of the new PDP.

## 6.1 Main Image Presentation

The main image must appear in a refined product presentation stage.

Recommended characteristics:

- Warm neutral background: `var(--dandy-bg-stage)`.
- Consistent square image stage where appropriate.
- Product image centered visually.
- `object-fit: contain` for product packshots where suitable.
- No aggressive cropping.
- Proper proportions.
- Responsive image dimensions.
- Subtle rounded corners using Phase 1 radii.
- No unnecessary shadows or decorative frames.

The product itself must remain the focal point.

## 6.2 Multiple Images — Only When Genuine Data Exists

If the current product data provides multiple genuine images:

- Display one main selected image.
- Provide a thumbnail gallery.
- Show the selected thumbnail clearly.
- Allow the customer to switch images.
- Update the main image without reloading the page.
- Provide appropriate accessible labels.
- Preserve correct product-image associations.

If only one image exists:

- Display the image elegantly.
- Provide image zoom or lightbox functionality where appropriate.
- Do not duplicate the same image into multiple fake thumbnails.
- Do not use unrelated category images as additional product photographs.
- Do not generate fake product angles or ingredient images.

The component must gracefully support both single-image and multiple-image products.

## 6.3 Product Image Zoom / Lightbox

Implement an accessible image viewing experience.

Requirements:

- Open image in a refined lightbox or native dialog.
- Close button.
- Escape-key support.
- Clicking the backdrop closes the dialog where appropriate.
- Keyboard accessibility.
- Focus management and restoration.
- Responsive image scaling.
- No layout shifts.

Do not introduce an unnecessary large gallery dependency.

If the current project already has a suitable image-viewing utility, evaluate whether it can be reused.

Embla Carousel is optional and should only be introduced if the verified image-gallery experience genuinely requires carousel functionality.

Do not install dependencies simply because they appear in the blueprint.

## 6.4 Gallery Responsive Behavior

Desktop:

- Large main image.
- Thumbnail strip below the main image when multiple photographs exist.
- Balanced spacing.
- Optional sticky gallery behavior if it does not cause overlap.

Mobile:

- Full-width image stage.
- Horizontal, touch-friendly thumbnail navigation when multiple images exist.
- Clear active-image indicator.
- No horizontal page overflow.
- No controls covering the product itself.

