## 7.1 Product Title

Use the approved Arabic typography system.

The title should be visually prominent without dominating the entire page.

Support long Arabic product names gracefully.

Do not truncate the product name when doing so would hide important identifying information.

## 7.2 Rating

Show rating only when genuine review information is available.

Preserve the Phase 3 rule:

A default rating value without an actual review count must not be displayed as genuine social proof.

Where supported, display:

- Average rating.
- Number of actual reviews.
- A link to the reviews section.

Do not manufacture ratings or review counts.

## 7.3 Pricing and Discounts

Pricing correctness is critical.

Use existing project pricing utilities wherever possible.

Inspect how Phase 3 handles:

- Normal product prices.
- Original prices.
- Valid discounts.
- Pink Friday promotional pricing.
- Discount eligibility.

The PDP must display the same valid price that the customer sees in the product listing for the same product and campaign state.

Do not implement an independent discount formula.

Do not duplicate Pink Friday logic.

Do not alter currency calculations.

Use consistent Egyptian Pound formatting and appropriate numeric typography.

Show the original price only when the original value is genuinely greater than the current applicable price and the underlying discount state supports it.

Do not display misleading savings percentages.

**Important:** If the listing card, product page, and cart currently calculate or display different prices, identify the discrepancy and document it. Do not silently change the financial logic.

